FactionBackstory (
    faction_id: "husks",
    canonical_name: "The Husks of the Fallen",
    motto: "We remember.",
    summary: "The remnants of fallen pre-collapse colonies, bound together by ancestor memory shards carried in glass vials around their necks. Bleached bone-white wraps over scarred armor; blood-red ritual markings; no negotiation, no surrender, no mercy.",
    history: "Before the collapse, there were colonies. Mars had three. The Moon had eleven. Europa had a single drilling station of two hundred and ninety souls. In the year of the orbital insurgency, the colonies were cut off, in stages, from the supply lanes that kept them alive. Some surrendered. Some assimilated. Some held out long enough to consume their own dead, and then their own dying, and then to forget which was which.\n\nThe Husks are not the descendants of the colonies. They are the colonies. Husk biology is human in the strict sense, but it has been re-routed through three generations of ritual consumption, ancestor-shard implantation, and selective starvation. A Husk warrior is born already remembering the death of a grandparent it never met; the memory is encoded in the silicate dust suspended in the small glass vial that hangs at its throat. When a Husk dies in battle, the vial is taken by the killer. When a Husk wins, the vial is added to the wearer's chain. A senior Bone-Crown matriarch will carry between forty and ninety vials at any time. The weight is, in every sense, the credential.\n\nThe Coalition discovered the first Husk cells in 2161 during the Mars Recovery Operation, when a sweep team found a colony that should have been dead for forty years and was not. The encounter killed eleven Coalition marines and produced no captives. The second encounter killed forty-three. The third produced a single survivor, who refused to speak for nine months and then asked, in a recorded statement, that the Husks be left to themselves. The Coalition denied the request. The Husks have not, in eighty years, asked again.\n\nThe modern Husks are spread across Mars, Vulcan, and the deep Europa cavern network. They do not trade. They do not negotiate. They speak in grunts, ritual chants, and recited names of the dead. The Combine has learned to recite Husk names faster than the Husks can; this is the only known counter-tactic that works reliably. The Husks remember everything that has been taken from them, and they have decided that the universe owes them the rest of itself.",
    philosophy: "We remember. Every loss is recorded in a shard, every shard is carried, every carrier is a witness. The Husks do not believe in justice; they believe in record-keeping. When a Husk burns a Coalition outpost, it is not a strike; it is an entry in a ledger that has been open for two hundred years. The Husks do not seek victory. They seek closure. Closure has not yet been achieved.",
    relationships: [
        FactionRelation (other: "coalition", stance: "extermination_doctrine", notes: "The Coalition does not negotiate with the Husks. The Husks do not negotiate with anyone. After-action reports use the same language on both sides — clearance, sweep, expended. The Husks consider the Coalition's vocabulary an insult, which is why they have repurposed it."),
        FactionRelation (other: "frontier", stance: "active_hostility", notes: "The Frontier's underground network is the closest thing the Husks have to a rival territory. Tunnel skirmishes are continuous; the body count is updated weekly on a chalkboard outside Olympus. The Husks have not won. The Husks have not stopped trying."),
        FactionRelation (other: "ronin", stance: "ritual_extermination", notes: "Ronin masters recite Husk names before engaging. The recitation breaks the Husks' fighting rhythm — the names are taken without being earned, which is the only thing a Husk warrior is forbidden by ritual to allow. The Husks have learned to flee from the recitation; the Combine has learned to recite faster."),
        FactionRelation (other: "synth", stance: "predictive_target", notes: "The Synth Collective models Husk movements as a stochastic graph of grudges. Synth predictions of Husk raids have a 0.41 success ratio, which is below the Collective's threshold for direct engagement. The work is contracted to Coalition forces in 78% of cases. The Husks have never noticed; the Husks do not care who pulls the trigger."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collective", stance: "spiritual_grief", notes: "Husk raids on Crystalfold settlements have decreased 62% over the last decade. The Crystalfold believe the Husks are sorry. The Husks have not commented. They have also not raided. The data speaks."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collegium", stance: "research_prey", notes: "The Collegium has captured three Husks alive in eighty years. None survived more than four months in custody. The samples are still being studied; the Husks have not retaliated for the captures, which is the only thing about the arrangement that puzzles the Collegium."),
        FactionRelation (other: "starlight", stance: "avoidance_pact", notes: "Starlight survey routes do not enter Husk territory. The Husks do not interfere with Starlight ships in transit. The arrangement is not written down. It has held for thirty-one years."),
    ],
    territory: "Mars underground (deep tunnels beneath the Frontier network); Vulcan magma caverns; the deep Europa cryogenic cavern system; an unknown number of derelict colony sites across the inner planets, claimed by ritual occupation and not by any treaty.",
    aesthetic: "Bleached bone-white wraps over scarred and improvised armor. Blood-red ritual markings applied in animal or human blood, depending on availability and ceremony. Glass vials of silicate ancestor-shard dust worn at the throat on woven chains. Helmets are often made from bone or salvaged armor; some senior Husks wear no helmet at all and have ritual scarring across the entire face. Weapons are scavenged, modified, and frequently named. The faction emblem, when one is displayed, is a stylized human skull crowned with three bone shards, painted in red on the wearer's chest plate or carved directly into the bone of the wearer's face.",
    voice_characteristics: "Guttural. Slow. Heavy use of ritual phrases. Husk warriors speak primarily in grunts, growls, and the recited names of the dead; full sentences are rare and ceremonial. Senior Husks (Bone-Crowns, Memory-Drinkers, Last-Tongues) speak in a low, deliberate cadence and use first-person plural pronouns, because they are speaking on behalf of the shards they carry. The Husks do not joke. The Husks do not lie. The Husks count."
)
